.TH SENTINEL-LOADER 1 "March 2026" "Sentinel-CC v4.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sentinel-loader \- Sentinel-CC runtime policy enforcer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sentinel-loader
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIBINARY\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sentinel-loader
verifies the Ed25519 signature of a Sentinel-CC instrumented binary,
loads its embedded security policy into eBPF maps, and executes the
binary under kernel-level syscall enforcement.
.PP
The loader establishes a cryptographic chain of trust: it verifies that
the binary's .text section and policy sections (.sentinel, .sentinel_cfi,
.sentinel_imports) have not been tampered with since signing. It then
attaches 16 fentry hooks and 1 fork-tracking tracepoint to enforce the
policy at every security-sensitive syscall.
.PP
For dynamically-linked binaries with a \fB.sentinel_imports\fR section,
the loader performs call-graph analysis through libc to whitelist only
the syscall sites reachable from the binary's actual library calls,
achieving significant attack surface reduction.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version string and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit
Enable real-time audit event printing. Without this flag, only BLOCK
events are logged via bpf_printk (visible in /sys/kernel/debug/tracing/trace_pipe).
With \-\-audit, all events (ALLOW, BLOCK, CFI_OK, CFI_FAIL, NR_MISMATCH,
FORK_TRACK) are streamed to stdout via the BPF ring buffer.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit\-format= \fIFMT\fR
Set the audit output format. Valid values: \fBtext\fR (default) or \fBjson\fR.
JSON output includes ISO-8601 timestamps and is suitable for log aggregation pipelines.
.TP
.BR \-\-audit\-target= \fITGT\fR
Set the audit output destination. Valid values: \fBstdout\fR (default) or \fBsyslog\fR.
When syslog is selected, events are sent to the system log (facility LOG_DAEMON)
with BLOCK/CFI_FAIL/NR_MISMATCH at LOG_WARNING and ALLOW events at LOG_INFO.
.TP
.BR \-\-fexit
Enable post-syscall return value auditing via fexit BPF hooks. Implies \-\-audit.
Emits FEXIT events showing the return value of key syscalls (write, read, openat,
mmap, connect) after the kernel completes them.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Triggers a policy hot-reload. The loader re-reads the binary's .sentinel section
and updates BPF maps in-place without restarting the child process.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown: kills child, destroys BPF programs, exits.
.SH SECURITY
The loader sanitizes dangerous environment variables before executing the child
process. The following variables are removed from the child's environment:
\fBLD_PRELOAD\fR, \fBLD_LIBRARY_PATH\fR, \fBLD_AUDIT\fR.
A warning is printed if any of these are detected.
.SH PREREQUISITES
.TP
.B Root access
The loader requires root privileges for BPF program loading and ptrace.
.TP
.B Kernel Keyring
The Ed25519 public key must be loaded into the session keyring before execution:
.RS
.nf
sudo keyctl add user sentinel:pubkey "$(cat pub.pem)" @s
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B BTF Support
The kernel must expose BTF information at /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux for
fentry hook resolution.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Child process exited normally.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (signature verification failure, missing key, BPF load
failure, key revoked).
.TP
.B 128+N
Loader was killed by signal N.
.SH AUDIT OUTPUT
When \fB\-\-audit\fR is enabled, events are printed in the format:
.PP
.nf
[Audit] ACTION PID=<tgid> TID=<tid> SYS=<nr> RIP=0x<addr> Off=0x<off> Mod=<id>
.fi
.PP
Where ACTION is one of: ALLOW, BLOCK, CFI_OK, CFI_FAIL, NR_MISMATCH, FORK_TRACK.
.SH ENFORCED SYSCALLS
The following syscalls are hooked via fentry:
write(1), read(0), openat(257), execve(59), mmap(9), mprotect(10),
connect(42), ptrace(101), memfd_create(319), process_vm_writev(311),
prctl(157), sendmsg(46), dup2(33), close(3), ioctl(16), seccomp(317).
.PP
Additionally, sched_process_fork is tracked via tracepoint for automatic
child process enrollment.
.PP
ptrace, process_vm_writev, and seccomp are \fBunconditionally blocked\fR
for all monitored processes.
.SH KEY REVOCATION
The loader checks /etc/sentinel/revoked_keys before accepting a signature.
Revoked keys are stored as SHA-256 fingerprints (one per line). Lines
starting with # are comments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B pub.pem
Ed25519 public key (loaded into kernel keyring).
.TP
.B /etc/sentinel/revoked_keys
Optional revocation list of SHA-256 key fingerprints.
.TP
.B /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux
Required for BPF fentry hook resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Basic execution
sudo sentinel-loader ./victim

# With audit output
sudo sentinel-loader --audit ./victim_phase2

# JSON audit format to syslog
sudo sentinel-loader --audit --audit-format=json --audit-target=syslog ./victim_phase2

# Pass arguments to the binary
sudo sentinel-loader ./myapp --config /etc/myapp.conf
.fi
